.TH CH-FASTSTART 1 "2026-07-21" "Agentic Sandbox" "Cloud Hypervisor Fast Start"
.SH NAME
ch-faststart \- prepare, attest, snapshot, restore, fork, and warm Cloud Hypervisor agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ch-faststart clean-prepare
.BI --vm " name " --host " address " --user " user"
.RI [ --identity " path" ]
.br
.B ch-faststart snapshot
.BI --vm " name " --id " id " --pre-enrollment --sign-key " fingerprint-or-key"
.br
.B ch-faststart restore
.BI --snapshot " id " --name " name"
.RI [ --instance-id " uuid" ]
.RI [ --mode " ondemand|copy" ]
.RI [ --wait-enrollment-ready ]
.br
.B ch-faststart fork
.BI --snapshot " id " --prefix " prefix " --count " n"
.RI [ --mode " ondemand|copy" ]
.RI [ --paused ]
.RI [ --wait-enrollment-ready ]
.br
.B ch-faststart fork-evidence
.BI --prefix " prefix " --count " n"
.RI [ --manifest " path" ]
.br
.B ch-faststart warm-init
.BI --snapshot " id " --size " n " --prefix " pool"
.br
.B ch-faststart warm-handoff
.BI --pool " pool " --name " name"
.RI [ --instance-id " uuid" ]
.RI [ --wait-enrollment-ready ]
.br
.B ch-faststart warm-status
.BI --pool " pool"
.br
.B ch-faststart warm-reconcile
.BI --pool " pool"
.br
.B ch-faststart verify
.BI --snapshot " id"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command is the CLI-first control surface for Cloud Hypervisor fast starts.
No resident orchestration service is required. Management uses the same
commands for its asynchronous API operations.
.PP
Clean snapshots are not created from a caller assertion. An operator first
runs
.B clean-prepare,
which stops the guest agent, checks that no TLS identity, bootstrap or OAuth
credential, credential mount, or agent process remains, removes virtiofs
devices, retains one credential-free NIC for restore-time rewriting, pauses
the VMM, and writes a short-lived host attestation.
The next
.B snapshot
consumes that attestation and requires exactly one NIC and no virtiofs devices
in captured CH state.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clean-prepare
Connect to the named base VM using non-interactive SSH, run the fail-closed
guest posture checks, detach credential-bearing devices, pause the VM, and
write a mode-0600, VM-and-disk-bound attestation. Host key checking is always
enabled. The command fails instead of prompting for SSH or sudo credentials.
.TP
.B snapshot
Capture a previously attested base. A clean base requires a detached OpenPGP
signature. Secret-bearing captures require the separate sealed-snapshot flow.
.TP
.B verify
Verify every manifest digest, require a good OpenPGP VALIDSIG status from the
fingerprint pinned by
.BR CH_SNAPSHOT_SIGNER_FINGERPRINT ,
and require clean-base posture metadata.
.TP
.B restore
Restore one child with a fresh disk, MAC, VSock CID, instance UUID, one-time
bootstrap token, guest-generated key, and mTLS certificate. With
.B --wait-enrollment-ready,
the CLI requires the guest's mode-0600 enrollment acknowledgement. Management
additionally requires the expected UUID to appear in its authenticated mTLS
registry before completing the operation.
.TP
.B fork
Restore all children concurrently. A partial launch is rolled back. RAM
metrics are sampled after all VMMs coexist and are scoped to the VMM's
.I /memfd:ch_ram
mappings. Snapshot-backing sharing is reported separately and is not counted
as resident guest-RAM sharing. Each child keeps its own enrollment metadata,
COW disk, CID, key, and certificate identity.
.B --paused
leaves all children paused for controlled evidence collection.
.TP
.B fork-evidence
Re-sample live children after fan-out, update the durable fork manifest, and
report the guest-RAM sharing verdict. Positive sharing is claimed only when
guest-RAM mapping identity or KSM evidence supports it; process-wide shared
libraries and the snapshot input file are excluded.
.TP
.B warm-init
Create real VMs from the clean snapshot, let each guest acquire networking and
mount its credential-free shares, then pause it. Tokens and leaf identities are
not staged in idle slots.
.TP
.B warm-handoff
Atomically claim a paused slot, bind it to the requested runtime and instance
identity, stage the one-time enrollment envelope, resume it, and asynchronously
replenish the pool.
.TP
.B warm-status
Print machine-readable pool and per-slot state.
.TP
.B warm-reconcile
Recover pool capacity by creating missing paused slots. It is safe to invoke
from an agent or a timer; pool mutation is serialized with an owner-side lock.
.SH TRUST AND CREDENTIAL BOUNDARIES
Bootstrap enrollment uses a dedicated HTTPS listener. The host delivers its
public CA through the isolated child inbox, the guest pins that CA for HTTPS,
and the returned leaf must match the requested SPIFFE URI, locally generated
private key, validity window, and CA signature before the token is removed.
.PP
Snapshot verification trusts only the externally configured signer
fingerprint. A key being present in the service keyring is insufficient.
Private keys never cross the guest boundary. Bootstrap inboxes are owner-only,
and successful identities persist under
.I /etc/agentic-sandbox/grpc-mtls
so service restarts and reboots do not fall back to cloned transport state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CH_SNAPSHOT_SIGNER_FINGERPRINT
Required 40-to-64 hexadecimal OpenPGP fingerprint accepted by restore, fork,
warm-pool, and verify operations.
.TP
.B CH_SNAPSHOT_SIGN_KEY
Key selector used only when creating signatures.
.TP
.B CH_RESTORE_LATENCY_BUDGET_MS
Maximum backend restore duration; default 1000 milliseconds.
.TP
.B CH_WARM_HANDOFF_READY_LATENCY_BUDGET_MS
Maximum paused-slot claim and resume duration; default 1000 milliseconds.
.TP
.B CH_ENROLLMENT_READY_TIMEOUT_MS
Maximum wait for a validated guest enrollment acknowledgement; default 30000
milliseconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/agentic-sandbox/vms/.ch-snapshots
Signed snapshot bundles.
.TP
.I /var/lib/agentic-sandbox/vms/.ch-warm-pool
Warm-pool inventory, locks, slot state, and reconciliation logs.
.TP
.I /etc/agentic-sandbox/grpc-mtls/agent.env
Restart-safe, non-secret path and identity configuration loaded by systemd.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the requested state transition and its local acceptance checks
completed. Nonzero is fail-closed; partial fork/restore children are destroyed
and management revokes any still-unconsumed bootstrap tokens.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grpc-ca-provider (1),
.BR agentic-mgmt (1)
